My very first NetHack ascension ever. Only took me ten years, too. :V

This one had gotten off to a nifty start: an early wish from a smoky
potion right after Sokoban got me an SDSM, which is secondarily what I
thank for my success. I primarily thank all the lovely gents in
#nethack on FreeNode, though, for sticking with me when things looked
damned grim on the Astral Plane.

So I walk in, Ring of Conflict on finger. Death is rather close;
fortunately, he's slow, so I run for the north room, tearing through
angels and whatnot along the way. He gets stuck behind the horde, so
thankful I didn't have to tango with him, I press on.

I run into Pestilence; he hits me before I get a chance to zap him,
making me Ill. No biggie, I apply my blessed unicorn horn.

Nothing happens. He makes me even more ill. I try again.

Nothing happens. Oh, dear. One more go.

Nothing happens.

At this point pretty much everyone in #nethack watching my game, self
included, pretty much said "Game Over." My soul prepared for death by
RNG karmic retribution on the next turn, I try to apply the horn again.

Success! And on a free turn from speed, too! I immediately head back,
quaff full healing (I was down to 20 or so of 170 or so), and plaster
him with a /oDeath from afar. What a save.

I make my way into the northern temple. Unfortunately, it isn't Odin's,
so I double back. Since Death is still trapped in the right corridor, I
head left, hoping it'll be Odin's temple. Getting caught in a massive
tangle, Famine makes his way in, and attacks me. You'd think the ring
of conflict would steer them away from me, but noooo.

Fortunately, I wipe him out in two combat rounds. Amazing, really--I
mean, I know that by the time I hit the Astral Plane I AM the Fourth
Rider, but come on, two combat rounds? Sheesh.

Anyway, it turned out I made the right choice going left; it was Odin's
temple. The rest, as they say, is melodramatically awesome history.

